B.aJF=new A.cv("record","How do I record something?","The gold microphone button, from anywhere in the app. It starts a new song and is recording from the tap (the first time, as soon as you have allowed the microphone) \u2014 no naming, no choosing where it lives. Press Done when you have it. You can do both afterwards, once there is something worth filing.\n\nOn a phone it works with no signal: the recording is kept on the phone first, and goes into Your music by itself when there is signal. One recording runs for up to 12 minutes, which is as long as a song here can hold, and the recorder says so while it is running.\n\nIf the idea is words and there is nowhere quiet to sing, press Write it down in the recorder instead. It is also first under New on Your music, and at the top of Ideas. On a phone what you type is kept on the phone as you type it, and goes into Ideas as a song named from its first line when you press Done, or by itself once there is signal.\n\nTo add a recording to a song you already have, open it and press Record on the toolbar. Once the song has a recording, the same button says New take. On a computer, with a song open beside Your music, the gold button says the same word and does the same thing; everywhere else it says New idea.",B.c5E)
