B.aJ6=new A.cv("take","How do I add a take to a song?","Open the song and press New take on the toolbar (Record, if the song has no recording yet). That adds a take alongside the ones already there.\n\nA take stays private to you until you share it. Press Takes to see all of them and share the one you want the room to hear \u2014 nothing you have not shared is ever audible to anybody, including on the Open Mic.\n\nWith no signal, a take is kept on the phone and shown on Takes as Not sent yet, with Try again. It goes up by itself when there is signal. If a take sounds late, open its levels and press Line it up to move it while it plays.",B.bx0)
B.dgm=s(["workspace_analyze_button","choose_reference_recording"],t.s)
B.bFn=s(["chord","chords","sheet","lyrics","words","key","tempo","bpm","transcribe","transcription","tab","analyse","analyze","notation","song"],t.s)
B.aJR=new A.cv("sheet","How do I get the chords and words for my song?","Record something first, then open the song and press Song Sheet.\n\nCoLabRoom listens to the recording, works out every chord, finds the key and the tempo, and writes down the words you sang \u2014 then puts the chords over the words. It takes a few minutes and it keeps going if you leave the screen.",B.bFn)
B.dfZ=s(["/settings/what-you-play","account_what_you_play_row","what_you_play_sheet"],t.s)
B.bZy=s(["ukulele","uke","bass","piano","keyboard","left","handed","lefty","shape","shapes","diagram","instrument","nashville","roman","sargam","jianpu","solfege","trumpet","sax","saxophone","horn","transpose","transposing","reading"],t.s)
B.aJ0=new A.cv("what-you-play","I play a ukulele, a bass or a piano, not a guitar.","Account \u2192 What you play and how you read.\n\nPick guitar, ukulele, bass or piano, and left-handed if you read a neck the other way round. Every chord diagram, sheet, chart and printed page follows it from then on. The same question is under any chord diagram and at the bottom of the tuner, so you can answer it where you are.\n\nThe same screen sets how you read: chords as letters, Nashville numbers or Roman numerals; sung notes as letters, do-re-mi, fixed do, sargam or jianpu; and the written key of a transposing instrument, so a trumpet part reads in B\u266d without you moving every chord in your head.\n\nIt is kept with your account, so a new phone starts where the last one left off, and nobody else can see it \u2014 not your band, not a teacher. A song you have already set differently keeps its own setting.",B.bZy)
B.dg5=s(["song_audience_dial"],t.s)
B.bI8=s(["who","hear","private","privacy","public","visible","audience","secret","safe","sharing","permission","song"],t.s)
B.aJt=new A.cv("audience","Who can hear my song?","Look at the bar under the toolbar when a song is open. It always says who can hear it, and tapping it shows the whole picture:\n\n\u2022 Only you \u2014 nobody else is in the room it lives in\n\u2022 Your room \u2014 everybody in that room\n\u2022 People you asked \u2014 somebody invited to this one song\n\u2022 Anyone \u2014 it is on the Open Mic\n\nYou can move it back down at any time, and a take you have not shared stays private no matter where the song sits.",B.bI8)
B.dfl=s(["song_audience_dial","audience_open_mic_toggle"],t.s)
B.c4b=s(["open","mic","publish","post","share","public","everybody","upload","showcase","song"],t.s)
B.aJq=new A.cv("openmic","How do I put a song on the Open Mic?",'Open the song, tap the bar that says who can hear it, then "Put it on the Open Mic".\n\nAny adult signed in can then find it, listen, and offer to play on it. Only the takes your room has already heard become audible \u2014 never one you are still working on privately. The same bar takes it back down whenever you like.',B.c4b)
B.c8W=s(["take","off","remove","delete","down","unpublish","hide","undo","mic","song"],t.s)
B.aJ8=new A.cv("takedown","How do I take a song off the Open Mic?",'Open the song, tap the bar that says who can hear it, then "Take it off the Open Mic". It stops being findable immediately.\n\nNothing you did while it was up is lost \u2014 the song, the takes and the song sheet all stay exactly as they were.',B.c8W)
