B.bGG=s(["sounds","like","genre","style","taste","tags","profile","describe","match","matching"],t.s)
B.aJH=new A.cv("sounds-like",'What does "sounds like" do on my profile?','It is how the app finds people making the kind of music you make. "Guitarist" does not say whether you play metal or jazz; this does.\n\nNobody is ranked by it. It moves you sideways towards people in the same corner, never up or down past anybody. Set it in Account \u2192 Your Open Mic profile \u2192 Open Mic settings (the sliders in the corner). Five words at most \u2014 fewer and sharper works better than listing everything.',B.bGG)
B.bbU=s(["discoverable","found","find","visible","hidden","profile","appear","listed","city","location","search","open","mic","showing"],t.s)
B.aJr=new A.cv("discoverable","How do I show up in the Open Mic, or stop showing up?","Account \u2192 Your Open Mic profile \u2192 Open Mic settings (the sliders in the corner), then List me in Open Mic. It is off until you turn it on \u2014 nobody appears in the Open Mic without choosing to.\n\nThe same place decides who can see your city: nobody, only people you have made something with, or anybody browsing.",B.bbU)
B.df8=s(["/openmic","/openmic/notes","open_mic_leave_want","leave_want_your_notes","leave_want_send","profile_your_notes","/account","account_your_notes_row"],t.s)
B.bIf=s(["told","looking","joins","wanted","notes","left","turned"],t.s)
B.aJQ=new A.cv("leave-a-note","Can I be told when somebody I am looking for joins?",'Yes. On the Open Mic, tap "Leave a note". It is at the top of the list however many people your search found. Choose who you would like to meet (if you searched for one kind of player they are already chosen), add a line for yourself if you like, and leave it.\n\nWhen somebody who plays that lists themselves on the Open Mic, you get a notification with their name, and tapping it opens their page. If you both show a town it has to be the same town, spelled the same way apart from capitals; if either of you shows none, the town does not come into it. Nobody is told who left a note.\n\nA note lasts a month. "Your notes", at the foot of the same sheet, is where you change one or take it down. It is in Account too, as "Notes you left on the Open Mic", and your own profile lists them.',B.bIf)
B.dfk=s(["sets_empty_new","play_the_set","share_set_pdf","the_bands_sets","give_set_to_room","live_previous_in_set","live_running_order","set_carry_on"],t.s)
B.bRo=s(["set","sets","setlist","setlists","list","gig","order","practice","performance","live","dep","sub","chart","key","tempo","form","ending","play","long","length","duration","minutes","slot","print","pdf","share","make","give","bandmates"],t.s)
B.aJS=new A.cv("sets","How do I make a set list?","In Your music, press New, then Set. Your sets are under Sets, beside Songs and Rooms.\n\nA set is a running order for one occasion \u2014 Friday practice, Saturday's show \u2014 built from songs you already have, in whatever order you will play them.\n\nEach row carries the key you do it in, the tempo, the count-in, the form, how it ends and a note. Key and notes on the row opens all six. Leave a field empty and the set uses what the song says.\n\nPlay the set walks the running order one song at a time, in the set's keys, with its tempo and notes on the stand, Previous and Next, and the recording off. Play from here starts part way down; leave a song early and Carry on takes you back to it.\n\nThe set adds up how long it runs. A length it measured from a recording and one it is working out are shown differently, and the total says how many of them are guesses. A song with nothing to go on has no length and is left out. A song whose sheet your phone has not been able to read says that instead, and the total says how many are still missing. The time between songs is never counted.\n\nHand this out gives you the three ways out of the app: print it, send the pack as a PDF with a chord chart for every song in the keys you play them in, or send the running order as text.\n\nA set can be the whole band\u2019s. Open the room: The band\u2019s sets is beside its songs. Everybody in the room sees the same running order, keys and notes on their own phone, and the room\u2019s owner and everybody who can record and edit can change it. The set says who changed it last, and never who opened it. When you open it, it fetches the latest and says what changed since your phone last had it; with no signal it shows the copy on your phone and says from when.\n\nTo make one of your own sets the band\u2019s, open it and press Give this set to the room. Every song in it has to be one of that room\u2019s songs first. From then on it is the room\u2019s: only the room\u2019s owner, or somebody who can record and edit, can give it back, from the set\u2019s \u22ee menu.",B.bRo)
B.dfW=s(["live_recording"],t.s)
B.bVQ=s(["silent","speaker","playback","backing","loud"],t.s)
B.aIV=new A.cv("perform-silent","Can Perform be silent, with nothing coming out of the speaker?","Yes. In Perform, the switch beside Start says Recording on or Recording off; tap it. With the recording off nothing comes out of the phone, and the words still move in time with the song \u2014 the count-in, the beat you feel and the chords called out loud all carry on. Your phone remembers it.\n\nA set opens with the recording off, so on a stage only the words move, and your phone remembers what you choose for sets separately.",B.bVQ)
B.dg6=s(["song_keep_here","keep_set_here"],t.s)
B.bXm=s(["offline","signal","airplane","aeroplane","wifi","internet","reception","basement","van","kept","song","perform","phone","keep"],t.s)
B.aJE=new A.cv("offline","Can I play a song where there is no signal?","Yes, if you keep it on your phone first. Open the song, press the \u22ee menu and choose Keep on this phone. A set has the same thing in its own \u22ee menu, and keeps every song in it \u2014 it says how much space that will take before it takes it, and once the day a set was for has passed it offers to take those songs back off.\n\nThat fetches the words, the song sheet, the recording and its separated parts, so Perform plays the song with its chords and beats with no connection at all. The menu then says On this phone, and a small phone sits beside the name of the song; press the menu entry again to take the song off.\n\nIf the app cannot open because there is no signal, the songs you kept are listed on that screen, ready to perform, and so are the sets you have opened on this phone, as this phone last had them, ready to play in order.\n\nIt is only for you and only on this phone: nobody in the room is told, and nobody else who signs in here sees them. A song that is not kept still opens with its words, and says that the recording is missing. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a song, so the menu does not offer it there.",B.bXm)
B.dft=s(["ideas_on_this_phone","ideas_on_this_phone_says"],t.s)
B.bKk=s(["recorded","sent","unsent","yet","waiting","upload","uploaded","uploading","plane","flight","signal","lost","phone"],t.s)
B.aJN=new A.cv("not-sent-yet","I recorded something with no signal. Where is it?","On your phone, and safe. At the top of Your music there is a row that says On this phone, not sent yet. It is only there while the phone is holding something.\n\nOpen it to play what you recorded, send it somewhere else with the share sheet, or delete it. Deleting removes it from the phone completely, and it was never anywhere else.\n\nYou do not have to do anything to send it. When there is signal it becomes a song in your Ideas room by itself, under the date and time you recorded it, and it takes its name from what you sang once you make its song sheet. If it cannot be sent for a reason that is not the signal, the row says why in one sentence, with Try again beside it.\n\nIf the app cannot open at all because there is no signal, the gold microphone button and the same row are on that screen too. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a recording, so recording there needs a connection.",B.bKk)
B.dg8=s(["songs_search_field"],t.s)
B.c_p=s(["find","lost","missing","gone","cannot","disappeared","search","song","deleted"],t.s)
B.aJn=new A.cv("missing-song","I cannot find a song I made.","Everything you have is in Your music, grouped by the room it lives in. If you cannot see it, use the search box \u2014 it matches titles, room names, and a lyric you remember.\n\nIf it was somebody else's song you were invited to, it is under their room rather than yours.",B.c_p)
B.dfG=s(["call_report","room_thread_more"],t.s)
B.bKz=s(["report","abuse","harassment","inappropriate","offensive","spam","copyright","stolen","complaint","flag","posted"],t.s)
B.aII=new A.cv("report","Somebody posted something they should not have.","Report it. There is a flag on a song's public page; on a person's profile, Report is under the \u22ee menu in the corner; on a room, Report this room is under its \u22ee menu; and in a call, press on the person.\n\nYou can also block somebody from their profile \u2014 you stop seeing each other completely, in both directions, and they are not told.\n\nA person reads every report, and you are told what they decided: Account, then Reports you made.",B.bKz)
B.dfv=s(["/settings/reports","account_reports_row"],t.s)
B.c2k=s(["reported","reports","reporting","answered","decided","decision","moderation","moderator","reviewed"],t.s)
B.aIL=new A.cv("after-report","What happens after I have reported something?","It goes to a person, not a machine. If it is about sexual content or music that is not theirs, an alarm goes off on our side once it has waited a day; for anything else, two days.\n\nIf you said it was sexual content on a profile, a picture, a song or a take, it goes to the front of the queue, and we take it out of other people's sight while somebody looks. Nothing is deleted while that happens.\n\nYou are told what was decided. Open Account, then Reports you made: each report shows what you wrote, that a person is looking at it, and then their answer. If whoever it belongs to deletes it first, your report is not deleted with it: you are told it is no longer here. You also get a notification when there is an answer; it says nothing about what you reported, so it is safe on a lock screen.\n\nThe person you reported is never told who reported them, and never sees what you wrote.",B.c2k)
B.dfD=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row"],t.s)
B.bTI=s(["refund","money","pay","paid","payment","charge","charged","cost","price","subscription","billing","cancel","free","premium","upgrade"],t.s)
B.aIS=new A.cv("refund","How do I get a refund? What does this cost?","Nothing. There is no paid tier and no way to pay for anything in CoLabRoom right now, so there is nothing to refund.\n\nIf you were charged by something calling itself CoLabRoom, it was not us \u2014 tell us at support@colabroom.com and do not pay it.",B.bTI)
B.dfj=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_credits","what_you_get_credit_history","analysis_depth_full"],t.s)
B.bPN=s(["credit","credits","balance","full","analysis","expire","lapse","monthly","many"],t.s)
B.aJB=new A.cv("credits","What is a credit, and how many do I have?","A credit is one full analysis of one recording: every instrument kept as its own track, and the song\u2019s parts named. Chords & lyrics never uses one, and running the full analysis again on a recording that has had one does not either.\n\nAccount \u2192 What you get says how many you have, and Where your credits went lists each one. Every account starts with a few that do not expire; a member gets more each month, and those do not carry over. If an analysis does not finish, its credit comes back by itself.\n\nThe Full analysis button says what it will use before you tap it.",B.bPN)
B.dfi=s(["analysis_depth_full","your_credits_here","share_my_credits_here","what_you_get_credit_history"],t.s)
B.c6n=s(["lend","lending","borrow","borrowing","use","using","let","credits","bandmates","yours","theirs"],t.s)
B.aJ1=new A.cv("use-one-of-mine","Can my band use my credits, or can I use a member\u2019s?",'Yes, in a band of up to eight, and only with a yes. If you have no credits of your own and a member is in the song\u2019s room, the Full analysis option offers Ask and their name. One tap sends them a notification naming the song, and they see that you asked.\n\nThe member answers from their inbox or the song: Just this once, Yes and let this room use mine from now on, or Not now. A yes spends one of their credits, never anybody else\u2019s, and their Where your credits went says which song and who asked.\n\nA member turns "from now on" off in the room: tap the line under its name that says how many people are in it, and it is at the bottom, under Your credits here. It turns itself off if the room grows past eight.',B.c6n)
B.dfB=s(["/account","room_thread_members"],t.s)
B.bMu=s(["delete","account","remove","close","quit","leave","erase","data","gdpr","deactivate"],t.s)
B.aIZ=new A.cv("delete-account","How do I delete my account?","Your account screen, at the bottom: Delete Account. It removes your profile, your words, and every room nobody else is in, with its songs. It cannot be undone.\n\nIf other people are in a room of yours, it is listed first, with two ways to settle it. Hand it over moves the room and every song in it to somebody in it, once they say yes. Close the room gives every song somebody else in it started, played on or wrote on to them, in a room of their own, and deletes the rest. Your account can be deleted once each room is settled.\n\nSongs you started and takes you shared in other people's rooms stay with their bands, without your name.",B.bMu)
B.dfe=s(["room_thread_members","hand_over_offer"],t.s)
B.c_N=s(["hand","handover","transfer","owner","ownership","give","role","permission","editor","viewer","commenter","promote","demote","admin","leader","band"],t.s)
B.aIT=new A.cv("hand-a-room-over","How do I hand a room over, or change what somebody can do?","Both are on the room\u2019s list of people. Open the room and tap the line under its name that says how many people are in it.\n\nUnder each person there is Change what they can do \u2014 record and edit, comment, or listen. It takes nothing away from them: their sets, their takes and the songs they are on all stay.\n\nUnder each person there is also Hand the room to them. They have to say yes: a card appears in their room and in their inbox, and nothing moves until they take it on. You can take the offer back until they answer, and it stops being offered after a fortnight.\n\nWhen they accept, the room and every song in it become theirs. You stay on and can still record and edit, unless you ticked Leave the room when they accept. Song sheets are counted against whoever makes them, so neither of your allowances changes.\n\nIf they already have a room or a song with the same name, the app says which and waits: one of them has to be renamed first. Nothing is ever renamed for you.\n\nBoth of you keep the same dated line about it on that list of people, and only the owner can hand a room on.",B.c_N)
B.dfQ=s(["/openmic"],t.s)
B.bI0=s(["demo","fake","bot","test","real","account","label","chip","seeded","nobody"],t.s)
B.aJG=new A.cv("demo","What is a DEMO account?","A seeded account, not a person. They exist so the app can be tested with a crowd in it before there is a real one.\n\nThey are always labelled, they will never answer you, and asking one to play on your song will not go anywhere. They are removed in batches as real people arrive.",B.bI0)
B.dfp=s(["/messages","messages_list"],t.s)
B.bVv=s(["message","messages","chat","thread","dm","talk","said","who"],t.s)
B.aIM=new A.cv("messages","Who can see my messages?","A message to one person is seen by the two of you. A line in a room's thread is seen by everybody in the room, including people who join later. Nothing you say is public.\n\nYou can write to somebody you are connected with or share a room with. Blocking somebody closes the thread between you in both directions.",B.bVv)
B.bIC=s(["take","back","delete","unsend","remove","edit","message","undo","sent"],t.s)
B.aJv=new A.cv("take-back","Can I take back something I said?","Yes. Every line you wrote \u2014 a message, a reply on an ask, a note \u2014 has Take back beside it. It goes for everybody, not only for you. There is no editing, on purpose: a changed line under somebody's answer would make the answer wrong.",B.bIC)
B.df4=s(["room_call_start","call_the_room_go","call_music","in_call_bar","call_whose","room_call_needs_somebody","person_thread_call"],t.s)
B.bwY=s(["call","calls","video","facetime","zoom","camera","ring","remote","webcam","rehearse","room","band","start"],t.s)
B.aJw=new A.cv("calls","How do I call my room?","Open the room and press Call the room, or Call on the room's thread, a song or a person. Everybody in the room is told, and joins from the room page, where it says who is already in.\n\nOn your own in a room, its page and its thread say Call the room: needs one more person, which opens Invite. In a thread with one person, Call rings the room the two of you share: straight in when it is just the two of you, and asked first when it is a band. With no room shared, it offers to start one, and you can call once they say yes.\n\nA call is for talking, watching each other play and rehearsing. It is not for playing live together: the others hear you a moment late. To play together, put the song up. Everybody plays to their own copy, and Record a pass keeps each person's part, lined up with the song afterwards.\n\nBack takes you to the room and the call carries on; the bar at the top brings you back, and Leave hangs up. Calls are for people 18 and over: the first time, you say the month and year you were born, once. The call itself is never recorded. No microphone or camera? You can still join, listen and watch. Playing along? Press Music mode and wear wired headphones.\n\nWhile a member of a room of up to eight is on its call, the call is on their membership, and it says so under the room's name. Nobody else's own calls are used while it is.",B.bwY)
B.dg2=s(["room_call_start","call_leave"],t.s)
B.c0m=s(["call","end","ended","ends","dropped","hung","stopped","disconnected","paused","kicked","itself","alone","timed","timeout"],t.s)
B.aJs=new A.cv("a-call-ended","Why did my call end by itself?","A call only ends by itself when nobody is using it. If you are the only one in it and nothing has happened for a while, a line at the bottom asks whether to keep waiting. If everybody has gone quiet for a long while, it asks whether to keep the call open. A call that has run a whole long day asks whether to keep going. One tap on the line carries on, and nothing ends while anybody is playing or while your phone is recording.\n\nIf nobody answers, the call ends and says why. Press Call the room to start another.\n\nCalls on an account can also pause until the first of the next month, after far more calling than a band rehearsing several nights a week does. If that has happened to you, ask here and we will lift it. Until then you can still be in a call a member of your room is on, because it is on their membership; it ends for you a few minutes after it stops being theirs, and says so first.",B.c0m)
B.dfc=s(["/your-code","meet_qr","meet_typed"],t.s)
B.bKt=s(["scan","qr","meet","met","gig","concert","connect","add","friend"],t.s)
B.aJK=new A.cv("your-code","How do I add somebody I just met?","Show them your code: Account \u2192 Your code, for meeting people, or the pencil on Messages. Their phone camera opens your card and they ask to add you; scan theirs back, or press Add back, and you are connected.\n\nCamera will not scan? Type their code (it looks like k7m2-9xqp) under Your code, or into Use a code in the inbox.",B.bKt)
B.dfS=s(["inbox_use_code","join_code_field"],t.s)
B.c4e=s(["code","link","paste","invitation","joining"],t.s)
B.aJD=new A.cv("join-code","Somebody gave me a code or a link. Where does it go?","Open the link and it takes you there. To type or paste it instead: the bell, then the key in the corner \u2014 Use a code. It takes an invitation, a teacher's lesson code, or somebody's own code. An invitation opens only for the address it was sent to; signed in with another, you can ask whoever sent it to send it again.",B.c4e)
B.dfd=s(["messages_new_lessons","lesson_new","lesson_poster","learn_teach"],t.s)
B.bKT=s(["teach","teacher","lesson","lessons","student","students","pupil","tutor","poster"],t.s)
B.aIH=new A.cv("lessons","How do I teach lessons in CoLabRoom?","Learn \u2192 Teach with a link, or Messages \u2192 the pencil \u2192 Teach: a lesson link. Each link is a QR code, which prints as a poster, and you can keep several, named for what they open: Tuesday beginners, Jazz studio. Every student who opens one gets their own room with you, private to the two of you. A link marked as a class also puts everybody who opens it in one room with the whole class, to listen; they still record in their own room with you. Lesson links are for students 18 and over for now.\n\nIn a lesson, open the song, press Perform, then Lead: your student presses Follow and their sheet moves with yours. What you worked on, and at what speed, waits for them on Your music afterwards, under Practise.",B.bKT)
B.dfn=s(["workspace_live_button","together_lead","together_follow"],t.s)
B.bXn=s(["follow","lead","leading","together","same","sync","scroll","perform","along","sleep","sleeps","asleep","awake","timeout","dim","dims","stand","phone","place","song"],t.s)
B.aJx=new A.cv("follow","How do we all see the same place in a song?",'Open the song on each phone and press Perform. One of you presses Lead; everybody else sees "\u2026 is leading this song" and presses Follow. The place in the song, the part on repeat and the speed then move for everybody together.\n\nWhile Perform is open, while you are in a call, and while a take is recording, the screen stays on by itself. It goes back to your usual timeout when you leave.',B.bXn)
B.dfE=s(["brief_reading_practise"],t.s)
B.c5b=s(["practise","practice","homework","speed","slow","slower","repeat","loop","teacher","left"],t.s)
B.aJa=new A.cv("practise","Where is the practice my teacher left?",'On Your music, in the cards at the top: "From \u2026" with the song, the parts and the speed, and Practise. It opens the song at those parts, at that speed. Close the card when you are done with it.',B.c5b)
B.dfq=s(["workspace_layers_button","moment_note_pin"],t.s)
B.c5l=s(["note","notes","moment","pin","pinned","comment","feedback","timestamp","playhead","mark"],t.s)
B.aJc=new A.cv("moment-note","How do I comment on one moment of a recording?",'Open the song, press Takes and play it. Under the buttons is "Note at 1:48" \u2014 the clock is wherever the playhead is, so stop on the part you mean and press it. On a laptop, N does the same.\n\nThe note shows as a mark on that recording and in the list underneath. Tapping it plays from three seconds before and goes round until you press stop. Only whoever played that take is told, and you can take your own notes back.',B.c5l)
B.dgf=s(["songs_tune_up","tune_up_tuner","live_tuner"],t.s)
B.b5j=s(["tuner","tune","tuning","sharp","flat","cents","string","strings","pitch","intonation"],t.s)
B.aIN=new A.cv("tuner","Where is the tuner?",'On Your music, under the heading: Tune up. It is on every song too \u2014 Tune up on the song\'s toolbar \u2014 and in Perform, in the list behind the timer button. Holding the gold Record button down opens it as well.\n\nNo song and no recording are needed. Play one string or sing one note and it names it, and says how far out you are in cents and in words: a little, quite or very flat or sharp. Once you have said what you play, it says which way to go as well: tighten or loosen on a guitar, ukulele or bass, up or down on a horn. Nothing you play is recorded.\n\nPlaying with a band at 442, or a baroque group at 415? Change "A = 440 Hz" under the needle. This phone remembers it, and the drone follows it.',B.b5j)
B.df9=s(["songs_tune_up","tune_up_metronome","live_metronome"],t.s)
B.bJB=s(["metronome","click","tempo","bpm","beats","pulse","counting"],t.s)
B.aJp=new A.cv("metronome","Where is the metronome?","On Your music, under the heading: Tune up, then Metronome. Also on every song through Tune up.\n\nIn Perform it is behind the timer button on a song with no beat of its own: words or a chart with no recording, or a recording nobody has made the song sheet for. A song whose sheet found its beat counts you in at that tempo instead.\n\nTap the tempo or slide to it, and choose how many beats are in a bar. Opened on a song whose recording has been analysed it starts at that song's tempo and says so; anywhere else it starts where you last left it.\n\nFrom Tune up it stops when you close it, so it can never land on a recording. In Perform it keeps going while you read, until you leave Perform. Takes has its own click for recording a part against. The click is not in the browser yet.",B.bJB)
B.dfX=s(["songs_tune_up","tune_up_drone","song_sheet_sound_the_one"],t.s)
B.bPy=s(["drone","tanpura","tonic","sa","held","warm","starting","fifth","sing","hear","note"],t.s)
B.aIY=new A.cv("drone","Can I hear one note to sing or tune against?",'Yes. On Your music, under the heading: Tune up, then Drone. Also on every song through Tune up, inside the tuner, and in Perform.\n\nOn a song whose key is known, the song sheet has "Sound the 1" under the title: it holds that note until you tap it again. Anywhere else you choose the note yourself \u2014 nothing is guessed about a song nobody has said the key of.\n\nChoosing a note sounds it. With no song open it keeps your note, so next time it opens on the same one.\n\n"Starting pitch" sounds it once, for coming in on. "Fifth" adds the note a tanpura or a pitch pipe sounds over it. The slider is how loud it sits under you. From Tune up it stops when you close it; in Perform it keeps going under the song until you leave Perform. It is only ever on your own phone \u2014 nobody else in the room hears it.',B.bPy)
B.dg_=s(["live_practice_row","live_tempo","live_page_loop"],t.s)
B.c1Y=s(["practise","practice","recorded","unrecorded","passage","loop","round","song","bars"],t.s)
B.aIU=new A.cv("practise-no-recording","Can I practise a song nobody has recorded?",'Yes. Open the song, press Perform, and the practice row is under Start on every song.\n\nWith no recording it holds Tempo, Count in and Loop. Tempo opens the metronome, where you tap the speed or slide to it; that number is used for this sitting and kept nowhere. Count in counts you in on that tempo \u2014 one bar, or two if you ask for two behind the timer button at the top. Loop asks which line the passage starts and ends on and how many bars it runs, and the page then comes round at your tempo.\n\nWith a recording nobody has made the song sheet for, the row holds the speeds and "Loop from here": press it where the passage starts, then again where it ends, and the recording goes round.\n\nWhat is missing is still in the row \u2014 Bars, Sing, Parts \u2014 and tapping one says what it needs. Most of them need the song sheet, and the sheet needs a recording.',B.c1Y)
B.dg1=s(["/settings/notifications","notify_messages"],t.s)
B.bXo=s(["notifications","notify","alerts","push","buzz","mute","quiet","silence","annoying"],t.s)
B.aJJ=new A.cv("notifications","How do I stop notifications, or get them?","Account \u2192 Notifications. Each kind has its own switch: invites, answers to your invites, being asked, messages, calls and new takes. Turning one off stops the announcement, not the thing: a message is still in Messages.\n\nNothing arriving on your phone at all? The same screen says whether this phone can be reached, and what to change if not.",B.bXo)
B.df5=s(["/","needs_the_phone_choose_a_file"],t.s)
B.c5D=s(["computer","laptop","desktop","browser","web","website","pc","mac","windows","chrome","use"],t.s)
B.aJz=new A.cv("web","Can I use CoLabRoom on a computer?","Yes: app.colabroom.com, signed in with the same account. Your rooms, songs, messages and calls are all there, and on a big screen the song sits beside the list. A recording you already have comes in as a file, for a song or as a take.\n\nA few things need the app on your phone: recording a song or a take, mixing takes together, the click, Feel the beat, saving a copy of the takes, sending a ChordPro file, and being told about things while the app is closed. On a computer, what is new is in the bell.",B.c5D)
B.dfy=s(["/people","people_strip"],t.s)
B.bL8=s(["people","friends","connections","bandmate","online","presence","green","dot","who","invisible"],t.s)
B.aJf=new A.cv("your-people","Who counts as my people?","Everybody you share a room with, and everybody who accepted a connection. A band-mate is one of your people whether or not they ever answered a request. Your people can see whether you have the app open right now, and you can see the same of them; nobody else can, and nobody you have blocked. To be seen by nobody, turn on Appear away in Account.\n\nFind them on the Messages tab \u2014 the row at the top \u2014 or under All, which is the People screen.",B.bL8)
B.dgi=s(["waiting_on_you","waiting_clear_all"],t.s)
B.bMX=s(["away","happened","missed","news","feed","cards","strip","unread","badge","inbox","cut","held","waiting","answered","bounce"],t.s)
B.aJC=new A.cv("what-came-in","How do I see what happened while I was away?","The row of cards at the top of Your music, which is the screen the app opens on. Whatever came in is there: a take somebody recorded on your song, playable from the card without opening anything; a mix or a bounce somebody sent back; a line of yours somebody cut, with the words on the card; and a song of yours that cannot go out yet because somebody with a part on it has not answered, with their names.\n\nNothing is counted. There is no unread number, no badge on the tab, and no record of what you have looked at. Each card has an x that clears it for good on this phone, Clear all clears the row, and everything goes by itself after a few weeks whether you touch it or not.\n\nNothing is lost when a card goes. A cut line stays on that song\u2019s own list, under Your cut lines in the song\u2019s menu; who a held song is waiting on stays on the song, under Who can hear it; and every take stays on the song\u2019s Takes screen.",B.bMX)
B.dfm=s(["workspace_layers_button","seal_take","seal_opens_on"],t.s)
B.c8j=s(["seal","sealed","sealing","capsule","bury","reopen","anniversary","later","away","given"],t.s)
B.aJi=new A.cv("sealed-take","Can I put a recording away and be given it back later?","Yes, on a take of your own that the room has not heard yet. Open the song, press Takes, and on that take's row press the sliders button \u2014 Seal it for later is at the bottom of the sheet that opens.\n\nYou choose the day it comes back: a year from now unless you say otherwise, and any day from tomorrow to just short of ten years. Until then it is off the takes screen and nobody else can see it, and it is not deleted.\n\nOn that day a card on Your music offers it back, once. Closing that card ends it for good; the take itself is still there.",B.c8j)
B.dfY=s(["workspace_layers_button","take_count_in","take_count_in_beat"],t.s)
B.bDU=s(["punch","punched","punching","middle","cold","count","song"],t.s)
B.aJ7=new A.cv("punch-in","Does it count me in when I record from the middle of a song?","Yes, once the song has a song sheet. Open the song, press Takes, move the playhead to where you want to come in, and press New take: the song plays one bar at its own tempo with a click over it, and you come in on the top of that bar rather than exactly where the playhead was sitting.\n\nA take from the beginning starts the way it always did \u2014 there is no bar before the top to count. So does a song with no song sheet: a bar counted at a guessed tempo would be confidently wrong, and this would rather say nothing.",B.bDU)
B.dfV=s(["workspace_layers_button","take_turns_start","take_turns_skip"],t.s)
B.bLY=s(["turns","swap","queue","conversation","skip","same","bars"],t.s)
B.aJ9=new A.cv("take-turns","Can we all have a go at the same few bars?","Yes. Open the song, press Takes, and under the part chips there is Take turns. Pick the passage in bars and the order, and anybody in the room can take one.\n\nEach person records over the same bars on their own phone, one after another, and the app lays the turns end to end so the whole thing plays back as one conversation. Skip me is always free and you can go again afterwards. Nothing about it is scored, counted or ranked.",B.bLY)
B.dfh=s(["live_loop_bars","live_this_is_bar_one","live_count_a_cycle","chart_this_is_bar_one"],t.s)
B.bOg=s(["downbeat","downbeats","cycle","sam","tala","struck","bar","bars","count"],t.s)
B.aIP=new A.cv("bar-one","The bar numbers are not the ones we count. Can I change them?",'Yes, and in two ways. Open the song, press Perform, then Bars.\n\n"This is bar 1" writes down where the band counts from, on the bar the picker is showing. Everybody in the room counts from there afterwards, and "Use the detected bars" puts it back.\n\n"Count a cycle" is for a song that does not go round in fours: tap how many beats it goes round in and which of them are struck hardest, and the sheet counts cycles instead of bars. It is offered only where a cycle would begin on a beat the recording actually has, because putting the 1 anywhere else would write down a beat nobody pointed at.\n\nA chart you brought carries the same "This is bar 1".',B.bOg)
B.dfs=s(["workspace_live_button","live_letters"],t.s)
B.bHK=s(["letter","letters","rehearsal","bridge","jump","start"],t.s)
B.aIQ=new A.cv("rehearsal-letters","How do we start from letter B?","Open the song and press Perform. Once the song sheet knows the song's parts, a row of letters sits above the transport \u2014 A, B, C, with I for an intro and O for an outro. The letter the song is in lights up as it plays, and one tap starts from that letter.\n\nThe same letters are on the printed chord chart and in a set's stand-in pack, so the letter somebody calls out is the letter on the paper in front of them.",B.bHK)
B.dgd=s(["copy_link_to_playhead","live_copy_moment","moment_note_pin"],t.s)
B.bID=s(["link","copy","clipboard","spot","exactly","exact"],t.s)
B.aJ5=new A.cv("moment-link","How do I send somebody the exact spot in a recording?",'Open the song, press Takes, stop where you mean, and press "Copy link to 1:48" \u2014 the clock is wherever you stopped. In Perform the same thing is "Copy link to here". Every note pinned to a moment carries its own link as well.\n\nWhat you paste opens the song at that second, on that recording, for anybody in the room. For anybody else it opens nothing and says so: there is no public page for anything inside a room.',B.bID)
B.dgk=s(["song_sheet_key_badge","key_reference_sheet"],t.s)
B.bLX=s(["capo","fret","frets","barre","clamp"],t.s)
B.aJd=new A.cv("capo","Where do I put the capo?","On the song sheet, tap the key beside the title. The sheet that opens lists the frets and what each one gives you, and the row for this song says it in this song's own chords: \"Capo 3 makes these open shapes: G, C, D\".\n\nIt is worked out for the instrument you said you play, so a ukulele gets the ukulele's answer rather than the guitar's. Choosing a capo there moves the shapes on the sheet and leaves the key the song sounds in alone.",B.bLX)
B.dgb=s(["song_sheet_sung_in","song_language_search","song_language_not_said"],t.s)
B.bOW=s(["language","languages","sung","arabic","hindi","spanish","song"],t.s)
B.aJO=new A.cv("song-language","How do I say what language a song is sung in?","On the song sheet, under the words, a line says what it is sung in. Tap it and pick a language, or type one that is not listed. Anybody who can edit the song can set it, and everybody in the room reads the same answer.\n\nNothing is guessed. Until somebody says, the line says nobody has. Once it is said, the app tells the transcriber which language to listen for instead of letting it decide from the first few seconds.",B.bOW)
B.dgj=s(["workspace_live_button","live_countdown_settings"],t.s)
B.c7p=s(["vibrate","vibration","vibrates","haptic","deaf","feel","tap","phone"],t.s)
B.aJ3=new A.cv("feel-the-beat","Can the phone tap the beat so I can feel it?","Yes, on a song whose sheet has been made. Open the song, press Perform, then the timer button at the top of the screen: Feel the beat taps the song's own beat while it plays, heavier on the 1.\n\nIt is off until you turn it on, it is on your own phone only, and nobody else in the room feels or hears anything.",B.c7p)
B.c2l=s(["spoken","speaks","aloud","ahead","coming","announced","blind"],t.s)
B.aJk=new A.cv("hear-the-chords","Can it say the chords aloud, a beat ahead?","Yes, on a song whose sheet has been made. Perform, then the timer button at the top: Hear the chords coming says the next chord a beat before it arrives, in whatever reading you are on \u2014 letters, Nashville numbers or numerals.\n\nOff until you turn it on, and on your own phone only.",B.c2l)
B.dfF=s(["bring_a_chart_door","bring_a_chart_paste","line_up_the_chart","practise_the_chart"],t.s)
B.c_h=s(["chart","chordpro","bring","brought","cover"],t.s)
B.aJU=new A.cv("brought-chart","I already know the chords. Can I bring my own chart?",'Yes. Open the song, press Song Sheet, and Bring a chart. Paste one, open a file, or type it: chords over the words, chords on their own, ChordPro, or chords written in brackets all read.\n\nA chart you find in a browser can be sent straight into CoLabRoom with the phone\'s own share button.\n\nWith a recording on the song, "Line it up with the recording" puts the chart on the beat so Perform can scroll it. Without a recording it still prints, and Perform still practises from it.',B.c_h)
B.dfr=s(["room_call_start","call_put_song_up","stage_song","stage_faces"],t.s)
B.bLW=s(["stage","faces","everyone","watch","together","song"],t.s)
B.aJm=new A.cv("the-stage","Can everyone on a call see the song together?","Yes. Open the room, press Call the room, and in the call press Put the song up. The song takes the screen \u2014 the chords and words moving in time, or the chart somebody brought \u2014 and the faces become a strip along the top.\n\nThe song never goes over the call. Each phone plays its own copy, so it is full quality for everybody; what travels is where the song is and how fast. How you read it stays yours, so a student can read numbers while the teacher reads chord names, on the same bar at the same second.",B.bLW)
B.dga=s(["stage_faces","stage_first_line"],t.s)
B.bPZ=s(["floor","loudest","duck","drowned","everybody","once"],t.s)
B.aJu=new A.cv("the-floor","Everybody is playing at once. Can one person be heard?","On the Stage, tap your own face: it says Take the floor. While you have it the other voices go under you rather than off, and tapping it again hands it back.\n\nTap somebody else's face to ask them to take it. Their phone accepts \u2014 nothing is switched on from your end, ever.",B.bPZ)
B.dfP=s(["call_walk_line","call_back_to_the_room"],t.s)
B.bEd=s(["walk","privately","aside","quietly","talk","student"],t.s)
B.aIR=new A.cv("walk-the-room","In a class, can I talk to one student without the rest hearing?","Yes, if you are the teacher. In the call, tap that person's tile: you step over to them and only the two of you hear each other. \"Back to the room\" brings you out again.\n\nEvery phone in the call shows a lamp on the tile of whoever the teacher is with, the student's own phone included. There is no silent listening in.",B.bEd)
B.dfU=s(["stage_record_a_pass","stage_hear_the_band","stage_pass_not_me"],t.s)
B.btX=s(["pass","apart","simultaneously","yourselves","part"],t.s)
B.aJy=new A.cv("the-pass","Can we each record our own part in one pass?","Yes, on the Stage. Press Record a pass: everybody who says yes records themselves, on their own phone, over the same part of the song. When it ends, Hear the band plays back what came in.\n\nNone of it goes over the call. Each phone places its own take against its own copy of the song, which is why the parts line up without any two phones ever agreeing on an instant. Anybody can say no to a pass, and then nothing on their phone records.",B.btX)
B.dfw=s(["live_we_said","we_said_body","song_what_we_said"],t.s)
B.bH2=s(["quote","quotes","agreed","decisions","decided","down","bar"],t.s)
B.aIK=new A.cv("we-said","How do we write down what the band decided about a bar?",'Open the song, press Perform, and press "We said" \u2014 it carries the bar you are on, so stop where you mean first. Type it, or hold the button and say it out loud into your own phone.\n\nWhat you leave is a quote with a name on it. Nothing summarises it, tidies it, turns it into an instruction or crosses it off: changing the chart stays a separate, deliberate act by somebody who can edit the song. Everything the band has said is listed on the song itself, under What we said.',B.bH2)
B.dgl=s(["/openmic","open_mic_play_with_me","play_along_words"],t.s)
B.bIq=s(["proposal","propose","stranger","strangers","ask","open","mic"],t.s)
B.aJj=new A.cv("play-with-me","Can I ask somebody from the Open Mic to play with me?",'Yes. Open the Open Mic, open their song, and press "Play this with me" under it. It proposes one session together on a call, on that song, rather than work they take away and do alone.\n\nThe terms are on the card before you send it and again before they answer: voice first with cameras off until each of you turns yours on, nothing recorded, and either of you can leave, which is the end of it. If they let it pass you are not told and nothing is kept.\n\nThe button is there whatever the answer would be \u2014 a door that appeared only for the people allowed through it would say out loud who they are. Both of you have to be adults.',B.bIq)
B.dgh=s(["add_gallery_pictures","add_video_link","video_url_field"],t.s)
B.c8i=s(["gallery","pictures","picture","photo","photos","videos","youtube"],t.s)
B.aJP=new A.cv("gallery-and-videos","Can I put pictures or videos on my page?","Yes. Account \u2192 Your Open Mic profile, and near the bottom of the page there is Add pictures and Add a video link. Both are there whether or not you have put anything up yet.\n\nA picture can be tied to one of your songs, and then tapping it plays the song. A video is a link to wherever it already lives: nothing is uploaded and nothing is hosted here.",B.c8i)
B.dgc=s(["call_add_camera","add_camera_qr","hands_begin"],t.s)
B.bOY=s(["hands","camera","fretboard","angle","tripod","overhead","fingers","phone"],t.s)
B.aJT=new A.cv("your-hands","Can a second phone show my hands on a call?","Yes. In the call, press Add a camera. A code comes up, and your own second phone's camera opens it \u2014 it has to be signed in as you. That phone joins as your hands, beside your face in the strip, and a tap puts it up large over the song.\n\nIt is never flipped left to right, because a mirrored fretboard is the wrong shape to copy.",B.bOY)
B.dfI=s(["song_who_was_in_the_room","split_keep","split_print"],t.s)
B.bj4=s(["split","splits","wrote","writers","cowriters","cowrote","royalties","shares","songwriting","publishing","sheet"],t.s)
B.aJh=new A.cv("splits","How do we work out who wrote the song and how to split it?","Open the song and press Who was in the room, on the song beside What we said. It lists everybody the room recorded on the song, with the lines each of them wrote and the takes each of them played beside their name. Nothing is counted or scored.\n\nUnder that is a draft of the writers' split. The room's owner, or somebody who can record and edit, marks who the writers are, including somebody who wrote the music and never typed a word. Everybody starts equal, and you change the numbers by hand until they add up to 100. It is about the song itself, not about a recording of it, and nobody signs anything here: Print makes a copy marked DRAFT to take into the conversation.\n\nOn somebody else's song there is nothing to split, and the page says so.",B.bj4)
B.dge=s(["/settings/licences","account_licences_row","auth_licences"],t.s)
B.biv=s(["licence","licences","license","licenses","source","attribution","acknowledgements","notices","typeface","fraunces","built"],t.s)
B.aJb=new A.cv("licences","Where are the open-source licences?","Account \u2192 Open-source licences, at the bottom of the list. It shows the licences of the open-source software this app is built from, and of its typeface, Fraunces.\n\nBefore you have an account, the same page is at the bottom of the sign-in screen.",B.biv)
B.dfT=s(["songs_ideas_door","ideas_kept_until","ideas_select","keep_it_for_later","take_keep_it_for_later"],t.s)
B.bKr=s(["ideas","kept","keep","later","thing","drafts","deleted","expire","forever","unsure","folder"],t.s)
B.aJ_=new A.cv("kept-for-later","Where is what I kept for later, and will my ideas be deleted?",'In Ideas, on Your music: first in the list of songs once you have any, and under the four ways in below "Start here" before then. What you record or write down with the gold button goes there, and so does anything you keep for later. Keep it for later is beside Throw it away when you cancel a recording, and beside Delete on a take you recorded, and what it keeps is named for the song it came from.\n\nNothing in Ideas is deleted by a clock. It is kept until you remove it: open Ideas and press the bin beside one, or Select to remove several, and it asks once before anything goes. Select can also move an idea into one of your rooms.\n\nUntil there is signal, something you kept is only on this phone, and a row at the top of Ideas says so; it goes in by itself when the signal is back. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a recording, so there Cancel throws it away.',B.bKr)
B.dgn=s(["/settings/blocked","account_blocked_row","call_block"],t.s)
B.bFO=s(["block","blocked","blocking","unblock","unblocking"],t.s)
B.aJA=new A.cv("blocked-people","How do I block somebody, or unblock them?","On their page, press the \u22ee at the top right, then Block. In a call, press the \u22ee in the corner of their picture. It asks once, and says what it does before it does it.\n\nAfter that they cannot find you, ask you or invite you to anything, and you do not see them either. They are never told. If you are in a room together, neither of you is taken out of it.\n\nTo undo it: Account \u2192 Blocked people, and Unblock beside their name. That does not tell them anything either.",B.bFO)
B.dfH=s(["/account","account_sign_out"],t.s)
B.bIk=s(["signout","logout","signedout","loggedout","logoff","signoff","signup"],t.s)
B.aIO=new A.cv("sign-out","How do I sign out?","Tap your picture or initials at the top right to open Account. Sign out is at the bottom, under the list, and it says Signing out while it works.\n\nSongs you kept on this phone for playing with no signal stay here, for when you sign back in; nobody else signing in sees them.\n\nTo make a different account, sign out first. On a phone, the sign-in screen has Create an account.",B.bIk)
B.dfz=s(["account_edit_profile","account_change_photo","account_face"],t.s)
B.bx_=s(["name","rename","avatar","photo","picture","initials","change"],t.s)
B.aJl=new A.cv("edit-profile","How do I change my name or my picture?","Account, in the card at the top: Edit profile changes your name. Beside it, Add photo sets your picture (Change photo once you have one), and Remove takes it off. You can also tap the circle itself.\n\nWhat you play, what you sound like and whether people can find you are on your Open Mic page: Account \u2192 Your Open Mic profile, then the tune button at the top right.",B.bx_)
B.dfo=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_standing"],t.s)
B.bit=s(["sheets","allowance","limit","quota","month","used","many"],t.s)
B.aIW=new A.cv("song-sheets-left","How many song sheets do I have left this month?","Account \u2192 What you get. The card at the top says which plan you are on, how many song sheets you have made this month and how many are left. They come back on the first of the month. If it could not check, it says so, and Try again asks again.\n\nA full analysis also uses a credit, and the same page says how many of those you have.",B.bit)
B.c4H=s(["plan","membership","stems","tier","tiers","member","add"],t.s)
B.aJe=new A.cv("member","What does a Member plan add?","Account \u2192 What you get puts the two side by side. A full analysis makes separated stems, so you can hear the bass on its own or mute it and play along, and names the song\u2019s parts on the sheet. Every account starts with a few credits for those, and Member adds more every month. And while a member is on a call in a room of up to eight, the call is on their membership rather than everybody else's.\n\nEverything else is free and stays free: rooms, recording, takes, the Open Mic, and the song sheet with chords over your words. There is no way to pay for Member in the app yet; the card says Later this year.",B.c4H)
B.df7=s(["call_music","call_put_song_up","stage_record_a_pass"],t.s)
B.bNr=s(["behind","lag","laggy","delay","delayed","latency","late","bluetooth"],t.s)
B.aJo=new A.cv("call-behind","The call feels behind. Why?","Sound on a call crosses the internet, so everybody hears everybody else a moment late. No app can take that away: it is the distance and the network. It is why a call is for talking, watching and rehearsing, not for playing live together.\n\nTwo things make it worse, and both can be fixed. Bluetooth headphones and speakers add a delay of their own that you can feel, so wear wired ones. And a weak signal adds more.\n\nTo play a song together, press Put the song up in the call, then Record a pass: each of you records on your own phone, against your own copy, and the parts line up afterwards.",B.bNr)
B.dfR=s(["account_email_password_row","change_email","change_password"],t.s)
B.bME=s(["password","email","address","forgot","reset","change"],t.s)
B.aJL=new A.cv("email-and-password","How do I change my email or password?","Account \u2192 Email and password. Change email sends a link to the new address, and nothing changes until you open it; if a link arrives at your old address too, open that one as well. Change password asks for the new one twice, and you stay signed in on this phone.\n\nSigned out and cannot remember it? On the sign-in screen, type your email and press Forgot password. The email that comes opens CoLabRoom to choose a new one, or to keep the one you have.",B.bME)
B.dfg=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_space","what_you_get_let_go","space_full_let_go"],t.s)
B.bHb=s(["space","storage","full","paying","gb","gigabyte","gigabytes"],t.s)
B.aIX=new A.cv("space","What happens when my space is full, or if I stop paying?","Every account has space for the recordings you add and the pictures on your page, and a member has a lot more. Account \u2192 What you get says how much of yours is used, with the exact figures one tap away. What the app makes from your recordings, such as stems, never counts, and nor does anything anybody else adds. A recording counts while it is yours to let go of: one you leave in a room you have left stays with that room and stops counting.\n\nWhen it is full, nothing is deleted, and everything you have still plays and downloads. Only adding new recordings waits: a take, an idea or a song\u2019s recording you make is kept on your phone, marked Only on this phone (a take says Not sent yet, on its song\u2019s Takes), and goes up by itself, to where you made it, once there is room. Choose what to let go lists your own recordings, largest first, and says what letting one go changes before anything goes.\n\nNobody can pay for anything yet. When membership arrives, stopping will work the same way: nothing you made is deleted or locked, and only adding new recordings waits until you are back within the free plan's space.",B.bHb)
B.dgg=s(["/learn","learn_use_code","learn_teach","learn_ask","learn_play_through","learn_learn_a_song","learn_teachers_near_you","learn_songs_you_can_use"],t.s)
B.c4s=s(["learn","learning","library","licensed","cleared"],t.s)
B.aJ2=new A.cv("learn","Where do I learn, find a teacher, or get songs to play?","Learn, the last tab. It starts with lessons: the people you teach and the people who teach you, each opening your room with them; Use a teacher's code, for a teacher's QR code or link; and Teach with a link, for your own. Ask about a song asks what the app worked out about one of your songs: the key, the chords, what might fit.\n\nTune up is the tuner, metronome and drone. Play a song through opens Perform on one of your songs, to slow it down, loop a passage and count yourself in. What you play is your instrument and how you read a chart. Learn a song brings the chords you already have, to read in your own key.\n\nTeachers near you and Songs you can use are not open yet, and say so there.",B.c4s)
